# MySQL safety

Set charset and collation explicitly on new tables to match the database
default already used in the repo (typically utf8mb4). Do not mix collations
in one join without a documented reason.

Do not use `LOCK TABLES` unless the surrounding migrations already require
it. Prefer InnoDB transactions for multi-statement changes.

Avoid `SELECT *` in new hot-path queries. Match existing index and engine
conventions.

Do not store secrets in SQL comments or seed data.
